---
// The Godot web export lives untouched at public/first-3d-game/ (re-export over it to update).
// It only loads after "Play" is pressed, because the engine download is ~38 MB.
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="First 3D game" description="A work-in-progress 3D game made in Godot by Nika. So far: a mage whose spells are drawn as seals, with six essences that blend into fifteen more." twin="nika">
  <section class="container section--tight">
    <p class="eyebrow">Games</p>
    <h1 class="title">First 3D game</h1>
    <p><a href="/nika/games">← All games</a></p>
    <p class="muted">A work in progress, built one feature at a time in Godot. So far: a mage in a forest whose spells are built as seals. A circle holds fire, frost, water, wind, lightning or earth; lines, rings and dots around it decide whether the spell flies, waits, spreads or repeats. Two different essences in one circle blend into a new element (fire and water make steam, wind and earth a rolling boulder), fifteen in all, and what they leave on the ground reacts with the next spell. Seals are put together from pieces by clicking, or drawn freehand (Tab on the board switches). Nine short lessons teach the marks one at a time. Needs a keyboard and mouse. The game is a ~38 MB download, so it only loads when you press Play.</p>
    <div class="stage card" data-stage>
      <button class="btn btn--accent play" type="button" data-play>▶ Play</button>
    </div>
    <p class="muted small">WASD or arrow keys to move, Shift to run, Space to jump. Click the game once to look around with the mouse; Esc frees it. Left click or F casts the chosen seal at the crosshair, 1 to 5 or the mouse wheel choose a seal, and Q opens the board where you change it. Press - and = to change how much mana you hold, or 0 for unlimited. T puts the lessons away, F2 switches to a flat training yard, M turns the sound off. Casting takes a moment: a bar fills with yellow beats on it, and a key pressed on a beat changes the spell (click again for a perfect cast, Z X C V B N to add an essence, E more bolts, R bigger, G on yourself). Character models by <a href="https://www.kaylousberg.com">Kay Lousberg</a> (KayKit, CC0).</p>
    <p><a href="/first-3d-game/">Open full screen ↗</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  document.querySelector('[data-play]')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const stage = document.querySelector('[data-stage]')!;
    const f = document.createElement('iframe');
    f.src = '/first-3d-game/';
    f.title = 'First 3D game';
    f.allow = 'fullscreen';
    stage.replaceChildren(f);
    f.focus();
  });
</script>
<style>
  .title { font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem); }
  .stage { margin: 24px 0 16px; padding: 0; overflow: hidden; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; max-height: 78vh; display: grid; place-items: center; background: var(--accent-soft); }
  .stage :global(iframe) { width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; }
  .play { font-size: 1.2rem; min-height: 56px; padding-inline: 28px; }
  .small { font-size: 0.95rem; }
</style>
